WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.404 --> 00:00:03.860
Unit twenty-four. The Ethical Hacking Mindset!

2
00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:09.312
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:13.098
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:17.482
Today we learn about The Ethical Hacking Mindset. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:22.851
Ethical hacking. Say it with me. Ethical hacking!

6
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.956
Permission. Say it with me. Permission!

7
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.775
Vulnerability. Say it with me. Vulnerability!

8
00:00:41.284 --> 00:00:44.918
Report. Say it with me. Report!

9
00:00:48.446 --> 00:00:51.912
Law. Say it with me. Law!

10
00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.343
Security. Say it with me. Security!

11
00:01:02.779 --> 00:01:06.313
Test. Say it with me. Test!

12
00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:14.504
Responsibility. Say it with me. Responsibility!

13
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:29.185
Ethical hacking means finding a vulnerability with permission so it can be fixed. Ethical hackers follow the law, test carefully, and report problems responsibly to improve security.

14
00:01:29.235 --> 00:01:32.564
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:33.351 --> 00:01:38.447
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:39.819
Vulnerability!

17
00:01:41.037 --> 00:01:46.290
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.490
Test!

19
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:55.431
Did you know? Testing someone's system without permission is illegal in many countries, even if you mean well!

20
00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.692
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:58.844 --> 00:02:07.695
Think and answer. Why is permission so important in security testing?

22
00:02:07.745 --> 00:02:08.896
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:15.336
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:15.386 --> 00:02:18.459
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

